+      "observation": "Retention/prune entry point that decides which lifecycle edges out of the current status are allowed. For each owned project it computes `terminalStatus = status === 'success' || status === 'failed' || status === 'fail'`, `terminalExpired` (>= FINAL_PROJECT_RETENTION_MS since projectTimestamp), `restoredExpired` (status 'archived', restoredAt > 0, >= RESTORED_PROJECT_RETENTION_MS) and `archivedNeedsUnload` (status 'archived', restoredAt === 0, at least one member agent currently loaded). If none of the three gates hold, the project goes to `skipped`/`kept` and no transition is attempted (line 177-180). Only when a gate holds is `wattclaw.team.project.archive` called (line 186), and a cold archived project whose agents are not loaded is reported as archived without any RPC (line 182-185). So the allowed edges are terminal->archived (after 3 days), restored-archived->archived (after 24h) and loaded cold-archived->archived; every non-terminal status (planning/in_progress/pending/creating/waiting/paused) and every not-yet-expired terminal status has a forbidden edge into archived."
